From b5410121d6df2c8bac35f368675fae22cb74ce9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 20:46:25 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] transports+configstore: PUT on
 /api/tenants/{tid}/{governance/virtual-keys,mcp/clients}/{id}
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds in-place mutation for the two simpler tenant-scoped entities so
operators can flip safe fields (VK active state / description / name;
MCP disabled flag / connection string / connection type) without
recreating the row. PUT on /api/tenants/{tid}/providers/{provider}
follows in a separate patch — UpdateProvider has heavy VKPC-resync
logic that needs its own review pass.

configstore additions (delegate-then-verify; tenant_id re-pinned on
the row before delegating so a malicious payload cannot move the row
into another tenant's scope):
- ConfigStore.UpdateVirtualKeyForTenant — verifies tenant ownership
  via GetVirtualKeyByIDForTenant, force-pins tenant_id, then delegates
  to UpdateVirtualKey (which preserves its existing id-or-name lookup
  shape because we set ID = existing.ID before calling).
- ConfigStore.UpdateMCPClientConfigForTenant — same shape for MCP.
- MockConfigStore stubs added (single-implementation delegation).
- Tests covering: own-tenant update visible to GET, cross-tenant
  attempt returns ErrNotFound and leaves the target row untouched,
  malicious tenant_id-in-payload defense.

Transport additions:
- handlers.TenantVirtualKeyHandler gains updateVirtualKey under
  PUT /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/virtual-keys/{vk_id}. Body has
  optional name/description/is_active; at least one must be present.
  Loads the row in the calling tenant's scope, applies the patch
  fields, delegates to UpdateVirtualKeyForTenant, then evicts the
  per-tenant runtime so cached VK metadata is dropped.
- handlers.TenantMCPHandler gains updateMCPClient under
  PUT /api/tenants/{tid}/mcp/clients/{client_id}. Body has optional
  disabled/connection_string/connection_type; same patch-apply-evict
  shape.
- Handler tests cover: happy-path PUT + evict, cross-tenant PUT 404
  with target unchanged, empty-body 400.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
